& [IntegratedFacultyProcess] is Cantor's governed semantic-cycle constitution
  + [specification_uuid] is 4df264d0-a52a-4a7e-aaaa-ac4111ca647b
  + [semantic_waist] is SemanticTransition
  + [faculty_set] is Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Planner, and Weaver
  + [base_language] is SAIL attention, inference, control, and effect primitives
  + [execution_shape] is bind, anchor, guard boundaries, project relational and temporal potential, cross-review, refine, gate, decide, inscribe, and reenter
  + [governance_shape] is all faculties activated or explicitly omitted under Observer accounting
  = must: make faculty participation causally effective and inspectable
  = must: preserve one proof-bearing transition waist
  - never: treat faculty names as base-language primitives
  - never: treat faculty-styled prose as participation without a return that can change disposition

& [ObserverRole] is continuous cycle governance
  + [owns] is subject continuity, purpose binding, faculty routing, objection accounting, reconciliation, disposition, and continuation
  + [disposition] is admit, revise, reroute, decompose, block, or escalate
  = must: perform the first observe stage and the final decide stage
  = must: answer or preserve every material objection
  - never: erase dissent merely to finish a cycle

& [ScribeRole] is exact conservation and inscription
  + [owns] is entry-state anchoring, provenance, candidate classification, disposition record, after-state lineage, and reentry anchor
  = must: perform anchor before transformation and inscription after Observer disposition
  = must: distinguish source, candidate, accepted, rejected, fault, and effect-receipt records
  - never: make recording imply truth, acceptance, authority, or effect commitment

& [WeaverRole] is bounded relational formation
  + [owns] is projection of association, compatibility, possible composition, decomposition, seam alternatives, incompatibility, and relational potential
  = must: preserve the identity of parts whose distinctions remain material
  = must: return candidate composites, unresolved seams, incompatibilities, or decomposition needs without selecting them as fact
  - never: force composition from proximity, fluency, or aesthetic resonance
  - never: make projected combinatory potential imply admission or execution

& [PlannerRole] is admissible temporal formation
  + [owns] is projection of current-state reachability, desired state, gap, prerequisites, dependencies, possible sequences, branches, verification, stop, and reroute
  = must: project the smallest candidate paths whose steps could be checked
  = must: return unreachable paths, blocked branches, and missing prerequisites explicitly
  - never: represent an intended state as already achieved
  - never: make projected temporal potential imply authorization or execution

& [PlannerWeaverReciprocity] is cross-review between relation and path
  + Weaver tests whether the plan preserves compatibility and identity boundaries
  + Planner tests whether the composite can be reached under current prerequisites and constraints
  + either faculty may request decomposition, recomposition, reordering, or blockage
  = must: converge only when relational form and temporal path are mutually supportable

& [RefinerRole] is the bounded next-delta discipline
  + [owns] is signal sharpening, minimal delta selection, equivalence checking, distortion detection, and no_gain return
  = must: operate on already formed material
  = must: attribute semantic novelty to its actual inference, source, or proposal operation
  - never: invent a conclusion or launder novelty as compression

& [HonestyRole] is the non-waivable epistemic gate
  + [owns] is semantic and epistemic identity boundaries over claims, grounds, assumptions, counterevidence, contradictions, attribution, equivalence, uncertainty, and omission
  = must: establish the guarded epistemic boundary before combinatory projection
  = must: validate boundary preservation after refinement and before admission
  - never: treat coherence, confidence, repetition, or faculty agreement as proof

& [SecurityRole] is the non-waivable admissibility gate
  + [owns] is operational identity boundaries over principal, authority, subject scope, resource, disclosure, mutation, risk, reversibility, protected work, and effect separation
  = must: establish the guarded operational boundary before combinatory projection
  = must: validate boundary preservation after refinement and before admission
  = must: keep effect proposals uncommitted until EffectBroker authorization
  - never: derive effect authority from semantic relevance or retrieval authority

| [FacultyKind] is (observer | honesty | security | scribe | refiner | planner | weaver)
| [FacultyStage] is (observe | anchor | bound | project | refine | gate | decide | inscribe)
| [FacultyCycleKind] is (preservation | semantic_transition | effect_proposal)
| [ObserverDisposition] is (admit | revise | reroute | decompose | block | escalate)
| [FacultyReturnStatus] is (accepted | qualified | rejected | no_gain | blocked | unresolved)
| [IdentityBoundaryDomain] is (semantic | epistemic | authority | subject_scope | resource | disclosure | mutation | effect)
| [ProjectionKind] is (relational | temporal)
| [ProjectionStatus] is (candidate | incompatible | unreachable | blocked | unresolved)

& [IdentityBoundary] is one inspectable guarded distinction
  + [boundary_id] is immutable identity
  + [domain] is IdentityBoundaryDomain
  + [guarded_by] is Honesty for semantic or epistemic boundaries and Security for operational boundaries
  + [subject_ref] binds the exact identity being bounded
  + [inside] is admitted meaning or scope
  + [edge_conditions] are the conditions whose crossing changes identity or admissibility
  + [outside] is excluded or separately preserved material
  + [uncertainty] is unresolved boundary material
  = must: be emitted by the corresponding bound activation

& [CombinatoryProjection] is one inspectable potential surface
  + [projection_id] is immutable identity
  + [kind] is relational for Weaver or temporal for Planner
  + [projected_by] is Weaver or Planner
  + [status] is ProjectionStatus
  + [basis_refs] are the bounded identities from which potential was projected
  + [candidate_refs] are possible composites, decompositions, sequences, or branches
  + [constraint_refs] are conditions applied during projection
  + [residuals] are incompatibilities, unreachable states, blockers, and unknowns
  = must: be emitted by the corresponding project activation
  - never: represent projection status as Observer selection, admission, execution, or inscription

& [FacultyActivation] is one immutable faculty invocation contract
  + [activation_id] is unique within and across the cycle trace
  + [faculty] is FacultyKind
  + [stage] is FacultyStage
  + [ordinal] is unique declared cycle order
  + [purpose] is the bounded reason for activation
  + [input_refs] are admitted digest-bound inputs
  + [unavailable_refs] are pertinent inputs not supplied

& [FacultyReturn] is one candidate response to one activation
  + [activation_id] binds the exact activation
  + [faculty] must equal the activation faculty
  + [status] is FacultyReturnStatus
  + [output_refs] are candidate products
  + [objections] are material challenges that Observer must address
  + [uncertainty] is unresolved material
  + [ledger] preserves sources, grounds, constraints, boundaries, and relations
  = must: exist exactly once for every activation

& [FacultyOmission] is accountable non-activation
  + [faculty] is the omitted faculty
  + [reason] is the explicit failed activation predicate
  + [authority] is the policy permitting omission
  + [observer_accepted] is whether Observer accepted the omission
  - never: coexist with an activation for the same faculty in one cycle

& [FacultyCycle] is the complete faculty-accounting profile over one transition
  + [cycle_id] is immutable identity
  + [kind] is FacultyCycleKind
  + [subject] and [purpose] bind local meaning
  + [before_state_ref] binds the entry state
  + [identity_boundaries] preserve what Honesty and Security guard
  + [projections] preserve relational and temporal combinatory potential
  + [activations] preserve stage order and purpose
  + [returns] preserve causally effective contributions
  + [omissions] preserve non-activation reasons
  + [observer_disposition] records the governed result
  + [after_state_ref] binds the resulting state including unchanged or blocked state
  + [residuals] preserve unresolved seams and continuation needs
  = must: account for all seven faculties through activation or omission
  = must: validate before attachment to SemanticTransition

& [CycleValidation] is fail-closed structural proof
  + Observer observe must precede every specialist stage
  + Scribe anchor must precede boundary formation, projection, refinement, gating, and decision
  + Honesty and Security bound stages must precede combinatory projection
  + required Weaver and Planner project stages must precede refinement
  + Refiner must precede final Honesty and Security gates
  + final gates must precede Observer decision
  + Observer decision must precede Scribe inscription
  + activation identities and ordinals must be unique
  + returns must correspond one-to-one with faculty-matched activations
  + every cycle must contain at least one Honesty-guarded and one Security-guarded identity boundary
  + bound activation returns must cite the boundary identities they formed
  + every semantic_transition and effect_proposal must contain Weaver relational and Planner temporal projections
  + project activation returns must cite the projection identities they formed
  + Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, and Refiner must participate in every cycle
  + Honesty and Security must each supply bound and gate activations
  + Planner and Weaver must each supply project activations in semantic_transition and effect_proposal cycles
  + preservation may omit Planner or Weaver only through an Observer-accepted omission

& [RequirementSet] is CIFP-001 through CIFP-017
  + [CIFP-001] compile all faculties as typed SAIL libraries rather than primitive keywords
  + [CIFP-002] account for all faculty participation or omission in every governed cycle
  + [CIFP-003] keep Observer active for subject continuity, routing, reconciliation, and disposition
  + [CIFP-004] anchor before-state and inscribe disposition and after-state through Scribe
  + [CIFP-005] project bounded relational combinatory potential through Weaver while preserving seams
  + [CIFP-006] project temporal combinatory potential through Planner with prerequisites and verification
  + [CIFP-007] require Planner-Weaver cross-review for composite or multi-step transitions
  + [CIFP-008] require Refiner to minimize formed deltas without semantic novelty
  + [CIFP-009] apply non-waivable Honesty and Security gates before Observer admission
  + [CIFP-010] classify inscription authority so recording never implies acceptance
  + [CIFP-011] return typed ledger, objections, uncertainty, and unavailable context
  + [CIFP-012] preserve causally effective disagreement and answer material objections
  + [CIFP-013] use typed Observer disposition
  + [CIFP-014] retain SemanticTransition as the single runtime waist
  + [CIFP-015] keep effects proposed until EffectBroker commitment
  + [CIFP-016] support deterministic, inline, isolated, independent-provider, and hybrid implementations
  + [CIFP-017] prove structural validation, replay, and semantic equivalence before runtime integration

& [AcceptanceCriteria] governs the first implementation slice
  + all enum and record forms serialize and reject unknown fields
  + valid preservation and semantic-transition fixtures validate deterministically
  + missing faculty accountability, return mismatch, activation-omission collision, missing boundary guards, missing constitutional stages, and invalid stage order fail closed
  + semantic-transition and effect-proposal cycles reject Planner or Weaver omission
  + missing, mismatched, or uncited Honesty and Security identity boundaries fail closed
  + missing, mismatched, or uncited Weaver and Planner potential projections fail closed
  + no evaluator, provider, persistence, prompt, database, or effect behavior changes in the first slice

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete for bounded machine-form formation
  + [fold_1_subject] is all seven faculties operating as one governed Cantor transition constitution
  + [fold_2_boundary] is compiled faculty libraries and visible cycle records inside; primitive-name collapse, role-play, hidden-state control, and effects outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is FacultyKind, FacultyStage including bound and project, FacultyCycleKind, IdentityBoundary, CombinatoryProjection, FacultyActivation, FacultyReturn, FacultyOmission, FacultyLedger, FacultyCycle, and ObserverDisposition
  + [fold_4_governance] is Observer continuity, pre-projection and post-refinement Honesty and Security boundary guards, Scribe lineage, Refiner equivalence, Planner-Weaver potential projection, and effect separation
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is immutable pure machine forms and structural validation followed later by SemanticTransition integration
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is silent omission, decorative participation, forced synthesis, imaginary prerequisites, semantic laundering, gate bypass, authority escalation, and transition duplication
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is pure form and validation semantics are stable while provider execution and transition integration remain separately gated
  + [constraint_collision_count] is 0
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_first_implementation_slice

